-<div class="notice" role="note"><strong>Experiment C20: shared tables and pooled registrations · implemented.</strong>Repeated registrations of one loaded resource append mutable rows to the same physical tables. The million-instance fixture now has six tables and 62,500 logical registrations. Pooled records track each registration's rows through 32-bit slot indices, preserving independent reset and unload. Different loaded resources remain separate. The public API and version 8 file format are unchanged. Flecs is v4.1.6-592-g9e874bca2, a development revision after the 4.1.6 tag.</div>
+<div class="notice" role="note"><strong>C21: query setup beside each benchmark.</strong>Light-color, health/position and Explosion define their Defold/Flecs queries in their own case files. Explosion owns a separate query: health is writable and position is read-only. Read-only scans declare both fields read-only in Flecs. Dense setup now creates five logical queries on all backends, instead of sharing the health query with Explosion; resource-instance setup still creates two. Creation and field binding remain outside timed traversal and are measured separately. Storage remains the C20 shared-table implementation. This is a benchmark setup change, not a runtime optimization.</div>
